This document describes how event-related information is structured and maintained within a system. It is intended for use in event management platforms, booking systems, or applications that display and manage event listings.
An event is identified by a unique event ID and includes essential details such as its name, description, and category. 
The event name represents the title that is visible to users, while the description provides a brief overview of what the event is about. 
The category helps classify the event into types such as business, entertainment, workshops, or conferences, making it easier to organize and search.

